%!PS
% Make the PDF: gswin64c -dBATCH -dNOPAUSE -dQUIET -dSAFER -sDEVICE=pdfwrite -dCompatibilityLevel=1.4 -sOutputFile=three_pages.pdf three_pages.ps
% Synthetic test document for PrismQDA's PDF import. All text is invented.
% Letter page, 12 pt Times (Latin-1 re-encoded), 14.4 pt line spacing, extra space between paragraphs.

% ISOLatin1Encoding puts a minus sign at 45 and accents where curly quotes belong; fix both.
/Enc ISOLatin1Encoding 256 array copy def
Enc 45 /hyphen put
Enc 147 /quotedblleft put
Enc 148 /quotedblright put

/Body
  /Times-Roman findfont dup length dict begin
  { 1 index /FID ne { def } { pop pop } ifelse } forall
  /Encoding Enc def currentdict end
  /BodyLatin1 exch definefont pop
/BodyLatin1 findfont 12 scalefont def

/Head
  /Times-Bold findfont 20 scalefont def

/Line { 72 exch moveto show } def   % usage: (text) y Line

% ---------------- page 1 ----------------
Head setfont
(Field Notes on a Neighbourhood Garden) 710 Line

Body setfont
(The garden opened in the spring of last year, after the council agreed to lease the) 670 Line
(empty lot beside the library. Volunteers cleared the rubble over two weekends and) 655.6 Line
(built raised beds from reclaimed timber. By June the first tomatoes were ripening,) 641.2 Line
(and neighbours who had never spoken before were swapping seedlings over the fence.) 626.8 Line
(The group also wrote a short guide with practical informa-) 612.4 Line
(tion for newcomers, and aims to become self-) 598 Line
(sufficient in compost by next year.) 583.6 Line

(Zo\353 brought caf\351 con leche for the se\361or who waters the beds, and the na\357ve) 555 Line
(plan to share one hose soon grew into a rota. Everyone agreed that the biggest) 540.6 Line
(surprise was how much \(and how loudly\) people talked while they weeded.) 526.2 Line

(\223It feels like a village inside the city,\224 said one volunteer.) 497.6 Line

showpage

% ---------------- page 2: blank apart from a thin ruled line (no text) ----------------
0.5 setlinewidth
72 400 moveto 540 400 lineto stroke
showpage

% ---------------- page 3 ----------------
Head setfont
(Second Season) 710 Line

Body setfont
(In the second season the focus moved from building to sharing. A seed library now) 670 Line
(sits in a cabinet by the gate, and children from the primary school visit each) 655.6 Line
(Thursday to measure the beans.) 641.2 Line

(1. Seeds are shared on Saturdays.) 612.6 Line
(2. Compost is turned each week.) 598.2 Line

(The council has renewed the lease for five years.) 569.6 Line

showpage
